    "answer": {
      "short": "$5\\text{ cm}$ is the diameter, so the radius is $2.5\\text{ cm}$. The working incorrectly uses $5$ as the radius.",
      "worked": "The marked $5\\text{ cm}$ is the diameter, so $r=2.5\\text{ cm}$. The working uses $C=2\\pi r$ with the diameter in place of the radius, doubling the circumference.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\pi d\\\\C&=\\pi\\times5\\\\C&\\approx15.71\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
